+        // already resized `target` (read_InvertedLists does this for every list), and
+        // swapping in a different block there would throw away an allocation that has
+        // already been made and zeroed -- strictly worse than staying out of the way.
+        if (!beforeknown_size.has_value()) {
+            size_t size = 0;
